        {
          "path": "_m/s/s/x/4/valley-of-the-kings-wp/la-tombe-de-sethi-1er-kv-17-va.jpg",
          "filename": "La tombe de Sethi 1er (KV.17) (Vallée des Rois, Thèbes ouest) ceiling left.jpg",
          "caption": "On the wall at the back of the sarcophagus room is represented the 2nd hour of the Amdouat, On the ceiling, the celestial vault and its constellations.\nSéthi I is the 1st important King of the Ramsid era (1294-1279 BC. J.C.). He had many temples built, including the large hypostyle room of the temple of Amon in Karnak or the temple of millions of years in East Thebes.\nThe tomb of Séthi I was discovered by the Italian Belzoni in October 1817.\n\nIts design is completely new. A division is introduced between the upper and lower parts and especially the entire tomb (100m long) is decorated in painted relief.",
